=== part 3: current keyd config ===
default.conf
enthium
global
mirror
qwerty
reddragon.conf
symbols

--- /etc/keyd/default.conf ---
[ids]
*
# the mouse
046d:c08b
# reddragon
-062a:38b3
-062a:8555
# keyd_mirror_bridge
-0001:0001

-0000:0006


[main]
leftshift+rightshift = capslock
# fix copilot key
f23+leftshift+leftmeta = rightcontrol


# includes
include global
include enthium
include symbols
include qwerty
include mirror

--- /etc/keyd/reddragon.conf ---
[ids]
# the keyboard
062a:38b3
062a:8555

# keyd_mirror_bridge
0001:0001

include global
include enthium
include symbols
include qwerty
include mirror



[enthium:layout]
rightalt = layer(altgr)
# have space do mirror instead
space = lettermod(mirrored, space, 5, 200)
# have leftmeta do symbols instead
leftmeta = lettermod(symbols, enter, 5, 200)
kp4 = w

# keyd_mirror_bridge
f24 = layer(mirrored)

# for mode 3/gamemode
enter = layer(enthium_shift)
rightmeta = space
rightshift = overload(qwerty_control, escape)
rightcontrol = rightcontrol

# for qwerty mode/m4
f9 = noop
f10 = noop
f11 = noop
f12 = toggle(qwerty)
[qwerty]
f9 = toggle(qwerty)
f10 = toggle(qwerty)
f11 = toggle(qwerty)
f12 = noop
enter = enter
# leftalt
rightmeta = rightmeta
# rightalt
leftcontrol = rightcontrol
leftshift = layer(shift)
capslock = layer(control)

[symbols]
leftshift = layer(mirrored)

[mirrored]
kp4 = enter
rightalt = overload(qwerty, toggle(qwerty))

=== part 4: add exclusion to keyd config ===

Edit /etc/keyd/default.conf (or whichever .conf you actually use)
and ensure it has an [ids] section that excludes ydotool:

    [ids]
    *
    -2333:6666

If your config already has [ids] *, add the '-2333:6666' line.
If it has explicit IDs instead of '*', do nothing here — keyd
already isn't grabbing ydotool because it isn't in the include list.
If you don't have an [ids] section at all, prepend the three-line
block above to the file.

You can do this in any editor; example:

    sudoedit /etc/keyd/default.conf

After editing, reload keyd:

    sudo systemctl restart keyd

